/semantic.cljc:442:                     (-> parked\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:454:                                :value :yin/blocked\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:455:                                :blocked? true\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:472:  \"One round between continuations: poll the wait set, then run whatever\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:473:   woke. Entries here carry no :resume, so `engine/resume-from-run-queue`\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:474:   with this machine's restore function is what resumes them.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:477:    (or (engine/resume-from-run-queue v' semantic-restore) v')))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:480:(defn- resume-from-run-queue\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:484:  (engine/resume-from-run-queue state semantic-restore))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:492:   Woken entries stay pure data and are resumed explicitly through `resume-from-run-queue`, which dispatches the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:496:                   engine/active-continuation?\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:498:                   resume-from-run-queue))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:512:   :current-continuation :current-cont,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:594:                       :park [opcode]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:595:                       :resume [opcode (:yin.code/parked-id ia)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:596:                       :current-continuation [opcode]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:635:   Segment identity is stable: continuations, frames, and closures name\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:640:   continuation that names the id.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:676:   Phase 2 linearizer in front of it. Parked continuations survive a load, so\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:677:   one segment can resume another's. A segment id already holding different\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:689:           :blocked? false\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:748:            :blocked? false\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:765:         :blocked? false))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:792:  (blocked? [vm] (engine/vm-blocked? vm))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:798:  (continuation [vm] (:k vm)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:846:                                  :blocked? false}))\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:4:> **Status: Proposed / Deferred.** The Semantic VM's linear CESK state is theoretically sound as an architecture-agnostic continuation format, but true heterogeneous network migration requires addressing several critical defects identified in the 2026-09-14 architectural review. This revision (r3) incorporates r2's answers to that review's findings 1–19 and the subsequent owner ruling on §7.3's canonical form; §7.11 lists the acceptance blockers that keep this warning standing until an implementation phase closes each of them with tests.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:6:The Semantic VM's linear CESK state (`{:segment id, :pc n, :env E, :stack S, :k K}`) is proposed as the canonical exchange format for network-transparent continuations. Because this lowered representation resolves execution-order ambiguity inherent in the Universal AST, it provides a simpler target for specialized execution engines (e.g., WebAssembly, LLVM, hardware FPGA) to participate in the `datom.world` ecosystem.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:8:To safely \"lift on park\" and \"lower on resume\" across heterogeneous boundaries without violating host isolation or concurrency invariants, the following contracts must be fully specified before this feature is accepted:\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:10:1. **Safepoint Reconstruction Metadata:** `:yin.code/source` mappings are insufficient for state reconstruction. The safepoint set must be exactly the machine's parking transitions — including effect-producing `:call`s — and reconstruction metadata must separate what is derivable from the canonical code alone (stack *effects*, lexical *requirements*) from what is per-activation state only the frame can carry (absolute depths, captured environments). Foreign engines publish per-segment safepoint maps derived from the canonical stream so arbitrary hardware states can be predictably lifted into the canonical CESK format.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:12:3. **Dependency Closure & Context:** A parked fragment is not a complete configuration. The format must carry its complete scheduler context — required primitives *with profiles*, loaded modules, referenced parked records, the fresh-name counter, and the reachable store slice — discovered by a conservative fixed point that includes explicit store operands, and must restore into an **isolated execution store** so the receiver's own state cannot change resolution.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:13:4. **Ownership Arbitration:** Emitting a continuation does not transfer ownership. Exclusion requires a **grounded authority** — a resource the grantor's boundary actually possesses, named in the value, independent of carriers — plus an **exporting state** that fences the source before publication, and **effect fencing** with authority epochs and stable operation ids, because absence of a lapse record is never evidence of tenure.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:14:5. **Code Identity (Content Addressing):** Because tempids (`:segment 123`) are local to a single machine's database, continuations must refer to code via immutable, versioned semantic profiles — a **canonical instruction vector** (positional tuples, not EAV) whose address is computed over the loader's resolved interpretation, whose addressed payload is the vector itself, and whose interpretation is pinned by a contract stamp versioning the *complete* execution contract.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:37:## §7.1 Stance: a continuation is a value, not a session\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:39:The semantic VM already parks as pure data (`yin.vm.semantic.md` §3.5): a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:40:wait entry or a `:parked-continuation` record is `{segment pc env stack k}`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:53:| **Emitter** | lifts a parked configuration into a UCF value and appends it to a medium | nothing, once appended |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:64:not occurrence**: the same parked computation can be encoded more than once\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:78:UCF facts live under `:yin.k/*` (K for the continuation component of CESK).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:87:{:yin.k/type        :yin.k/continuation\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:91: :yin.k/origin      {:yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/o-…                        ; predecessor, or absent on a first park\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:98: :yin.k/scheduler   {…}                        ; §7.6.3  fresh-name state and referenced parked records\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:99: :yin.k/requires    {…}                        ; §7.6  dependency closure, with discovery status\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:105:The parts answer four questions a resumer must be able to ask of the data\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:106:alone: *what code* (`:yin.k/requires`, `:yin.k/carried`, and every segment\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:109:(`:yin.k/requires`, `:yin.k/arbitration`), and *who may run it*\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:136:`123` is different code or no code. A continuation naming code by tempid is\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:142:§2.2, becomes required on any segment a continuation may reference. Its\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:264:A resumer whose loader implements a different revision does not guess: it\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:267:resumer on the old one cannot run code that observes the difference, and the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:276:### 7.3.4 References to code inside a continuation\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:292:Loading a fetched vector has two paths, and both are specified. The\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:308:On lowering, the resumer resolves each address in this order and stops at the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:336:**The continuation's own identity and the occurrence.** `:yin.k/id` is the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:340:`(assoc body :yin.k/id (dao.jing/segment-key body))`. Equal continuations\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:344:occurrence id, minted exactly once, when a park is first exported, unique\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:346:snapshot variant and every retry of the same park (§7.7.2). A re-emission\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:358:UCF resolves this by rule rather than by metadata: **a continuation may be\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
